{
  "reviews": [
    {
      "reference": "1 Enoch 54:9",
      "verdict": "hold",
      "source_assessment": "body137-LIV.png places the unit after baseline 9 and before baseline 10, across the second and third body lines. The radial asterisk immediately before ዲበ is real; raised apparatus numerals 7–10 are not source words. No internal brackets are visible. The photographs support several corrections to my frozen provisional transcription, detailed below. The candidate retains the opening conjunction, quantifier, two relative inhabitant clauses, conjunction joining those clauses, starred locative expression, and terminal heaven expression. Nevertheless, the destruction predicate's exact morphological analysis is not established by identifying its root. I cannot certify the candidate's asserted active voice from the supplied evidence.",
      "translation_assessment": "The Latin photographs support dwelling, dry land, a lower spatial relation, extremities, and heaven. They do not, by themselves, establish the candidate's decisive wording 'they will wipe out.' The destruction entry distinguishes active extinction/destruction from passive extinction/destruction, and the passive entry includes a reference to Hen. 54,9. That reference is not a substitute for analysing the photographed Ethiopic form, but it makes the mandatory active-voice assertion especially unsuitable for approval without a resolved morphological control. The two inhabitant clauses and 'all' are represented in the English; no explicit negative or demonstrative is visible in the source. The complete locative construction, including ዲበ and the form and government of መትሕተ, still requires adequate control.",
      "note_assessment": "The identical source note and footnote are not approved. Their categorical assertion that the selected predicate is active exceeds the demonstrated evidence. Column numbers alone do not identify the actual photographic evidence or explain the relevant active/passive distinction. The footnote is labelled textual_variant, but the supplied body photographs show only an apparatus marker, not the associated apparatus explanation. Consequently, the note does not establish what the star signifies or which variant is being explained. Its claims about retaining a selected final-o quantifier and avoiding a passive substitution cannot resolve morphology by assertion.",
      "rationale": "This is a whole-unit hold, not a finding that the candidate is necessarily wrong. Photographic reinspection improves the frozen source reading, but lexical plausibility does not settle the destruction predicate's voice or the complete spatial construction. Missing or insufficiently readable controls prevent approval of the source, English, and mandatory explanation together.",
      "remaining_decisive_uncertainties": [
        "The exact stem, vocalization, voice, subject relation, and tense/aspect analysis of photographed ወይደመስሱ remain unresolved. The active root gloss and the passive entry must not be conflated.",
        "No identifiable complete original Dillmann photographic entry for ዲበ has been supplied; 'on/upon' therefore lacks the requested explicit primary lexical control.",
        "The precise grammatical status and government of photographed መትሕተ in relation to አጽናፈ ሰማይ are not established merely by the lower-region vocabulary in pp553.jpg and pp555.jpg.",
        "Some fine print in the dwelling entry and its continuation on pp613.jpg is insufficiently legible for me to claim the requested complete-entry verification.",
        "The Charles apparatus text associated with the asterisk before ዲበ is absent, preventing verification of the mandatory textual-variant explanation."
      ],
      "lexical_controls": [
        {
          "head": "ደመሰ and its passive derivative",
          "photo_filenames": [
            "pp1087.jpg",
            "pp1089.jpg"
          ],
          "actual_primary_Latin_support": "Column 1088 gives the quadriliteral root with 'extinguere, delere', including 'obliterare' and 'perdere'; the entry continues at the top of column 1089. Column 1089 separately gives passive support through 'deleri, extingui', 'obliterari', and 'perdi', with Hen. 54,9 among its references. These distinguish semantic and voice possibilities; they do not independently prove the candidate surface form active."
        },
        {
          "head": "ኀደረ",
          "photo_filenames": [
            "pp613.jpg"
          ],
          "actual_primary_Latin_support": "Columns 613–614 visibly support 'considere, domicilium vel tabernaculum collocare' and 'commorari, habitare, incolere'. The entry also distinguishes further stem uses. This supports dwelling vocabulary, but I cannot certify every small-print line of the relevant entry and continuation as read."
        },
        {
          "head": "ኵሉ and its forms",
          "photo_filenames": [
            "pp813.jpg",
            "pp815.jpg"
          ],
          "actual_primary_Latin_support": "The entry begins in column 814 and continues through columns 815–816. Visible support includes 'universitas', 'universum', 'omnia', 'omnis, omnes', and 'omnes et singuli'. Its discussion of pronominal and substantival uses supports totality, but a general gloss does not itself resolve every syntactic feature of photographed ኵሎ."
        },
        {
          "head": "የብስ",
          "photo_filenames": [
            "pp1071.jpg"
          ],
          "actual_primary_Latin_support": "The substantive entry spanning columns 1071–1072 gives 'aridum vel siccum i. e. terra vel continens', with the continuation 'siccitas, ariditas'. This directly supports 'dry land' in the candidate."
        },
        {
          "head": "ትሕት / መትሕት",
          "photo_filenames": [
            "pp553.jpg",
            "pp555.jpg"
          ],
          "actual_primary_Latin_support": "Column 554 includes 'pars inferior, quod infra est', 'infra, subter, subtus', and discussion of prepositional uses. Column 555 gives the related substantive 'pars vel locus inferior vel infimus'. These support a lower spatial relation, but do not alone establish the exact photographed form's construction with the following noun."
        },
        {
          "head": "ጽንፍ",
          "photo_filenames": [
            "pp1293.jpg",
            "pp1295.jpg"
          ],
          "actual_primary_Latin_support": "The entry begins in column 1294 with 'ora, margo vel labia', then distinguishes 'extremitas, finis, terminus'. Its continuation in column 1295 includes 'passim finis i. e. fines' and 'confinia'. This supports the extremities/ends sense; it does not supply a modern cosmological interpretation."
        },
        {
          "head": "ሰማይ",
          "photo_filenames": [
            "pp341.jpg"
          ],
          "actual_primary_Latin_support": "Column 341 identifies the substantive, its plural, and 'coelum'. This supports 'heaven' without adding an explanatory cosmology."
        },
        {
          "head": "ዲበ",
          "photo_filenames": [],
          "actual_primary_Latin_support": "No complete relevant entry is identifiable in the supplied Latin photographs. The candidate gloss is not accepted as primary evidence."
        }
      ],
      "changes_from_own_source_freeze": [
        "At the opening predicate, body137-LIV.png and the enlarged v9-all.png support reading the fidel immediately after መ as ስ rather than my frozen ሰ: ወይደመስሱ. The original Latin root entry in pp1087.jpg supplies a matching destruction root, but does not resolve this form's voice.",
        "At both inhabitant verbs—the word before *ዲበ on the second body line and the corresponding word after ወእለ on the third—body137-LIV.png supports ኀድ in place of my frozen ነብ, yielding የኀድሩ. The head and dwelling senses in pp613.jpg independently support this lexical identification.",
        "In the word immediately after the second inhabitant verb, body137-LIV.png supports final ተ rather than frozen ት, yielding መትሕተ. The lower-region entries in pp553.jpg and pp555.jpg support the lexical family, not a complete grammatical resolution.",
        "In the word immediately before ሰማይ, body137-LIV.png shows the four-fidel sequence አጽናፈ rather than my frozen three-fidel እግረ. The ጽንፍ entry and continuation in pp1293.jpg and pp1295.jpg independently support the extremities lexical identification.",
        "These are photograph-based corrections to provisional source readings, not adoption of the candidate's active-voice assertion or withdrawal of the whole-unit hold."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "limits": "Review limited to the supplied Charles body photographs and original Dillmann Latin photographs for 1 Enoch 54:9. No TEI/OCR glosses, remembered translations, neighboring-unit approval, manuscript or autograph certification, artwork approval, reader release, publication authorization, or whole-book verification is claimed.",
  "publication_approved": false,
  "full_book_verified": false
}
